1
00:02:04,315 --> 00:02:08,375
NO ANIMALS WERE HARMED DURING THE
FILMING OF THIS PRODUCTION

2
00:02:09,772 --> 00:02:19,822
Please contact us for any inquiries
turkision@gmail.com

3
00:02:31,190 --> 00:02:32,760
He is there!

4
00:02:38,060 --> 00:02:39,090
Osman!

5
00:02:40,660 --> 00:02:42,890
You are trapped just like a mouse!

6
00:02:45,090 --> 00:02:47,960
Give me the one who killed my unarmed
soldier!

7
00:02:48,090 --> 00:02:49,060
I want Göktuğ!

8
00:02:49,390 --> 00:02:50,890
I know he is with you!

9
00:02:51,290 --> 00:02:52,360
Flatyos…

10
00:02:53,990 --> 00:02:56,890
… did your man die because of a tiny bite…

11
00:02:57,760 --> 00:02:59,590
… or an incubus?

12
00:03:01,290 --> 00:03:02,560
Tell me!

13
00:03:03,360 --> 00:03:05,310
You are surrounded, Osman!

14
00:03:05,440 --> 00:03:07,160
If you want to live, give me Göktuğ!

15
00:03:07,310 --> 00:03:09,740
I took care of many dogs like you in the
past.

16
00:03:10,710 --> 00:03:12,040
Now it’s your turn.

17
00:03:13,140 --> 00:03:14,340
You are going to die!

18
00:03:15,940 --> 00:03:17,310
You will die.

19
00:04:19,480 --> 00:04:20,980
Bamsı Bey!

20
00:04:21,779 --> 00:04:23,350
My sturdy Osman.

21
00:04:51,380 --> 00:04:52,750
My Osman.

22
00:05:00,680 --> 00:05:03,280
I did what you ordered, my Bey.

23
00:05:03,480 --> 00:05:04,780
May you live long.

24
00:05:04,980 --> 00:05:10,380
Osman will hide Göktuğ till we are safe
from Geyhatu’s terror.

25
00:05:12,540 --> 00:05:14,750
With Allah’s permission…

26
00:05:16,080 --> 00:05:19,890
… we will defeat Geyhatu when Savcı
becomes victorious.

27
00:05:20,580 --> 00:05:22,380
With Allah’s permission, my Bey.

28
00:05:22,880 --> 00:05:24,650
With Allah’s permission.

29
00:05:28,580 --> 00:05:30,250
What’s wrong, Abdurrahman?

30
00:05:31,180 --> 00:05:32,550
My Bey…

31
00:05:33,450 --> 00:05:34,950
I said what’s wrong.

32
00:05:35,150 --> 00:05:37,380
… Osman Bey.

33
00:05:38,050 --> 00:05:39,680
What about him?

34
00:05:40,880 --> 00:05:42,650
Osman...

35
00:05:42,950 --> 00:05:46,550
… as if the ground split and he entered
the ground.

36
00:05:47,890 --> 00:05:50,690
I hope he listens to what I said…

37
00:05:52,390 --> 00:05:54,850
… and that he is not after his brother,
Savcı.

38
00:05:55,290 --> 00:05:56,350
Osman...

39
00:05:57,850 --> 00:06:00,490
… I hope he won’t make such mistakes.

40
00:06:10,450 --> 00:06:11,690
My son.

41
00:06:12,090 --> 00:06:13,190
My Bamsı Bey.

42
00:06:13,450 --> 00:06:16,250
-Allah is eternal!
-Allah is rightful!

43
00:06:22,850 --> 00:06:24,650
You will pay for this, Osman.

44
00:06:41,090 --> 00:06:42,960
My Bamsı Bey.

45
00:06:43,190 --> 00:06:44,890
Oh, my lion!

46
00:06:45,860 --> 00:06:47,960
Oh, my sturdy Osman!

47
00:06:50,260 --> 00:06:52,090
As if Allah sent you here.

48
00:06:52,560 --> 00:06:54,060
Where did you come here?

49
00:06:54,990 --> 00:06:58,290
Always look for the savior.

50
00:07:01,450 --> 00:07:04,790
Sturdy Osman, Ertugrul Gazi’s son!

51
00:07:04,890 --> 00:07:08,290
I see you are fighting against yet
another trouble.

52
00:07:08,390 --> 00:07:09,760
Where have you been?

53
00:07:10,390 --> 00:07:11,990
We missed you so much.

54
00:07:13,290 --> 00:07:16,190
I will tell you where, once we are at
the Tent.

55
00:07:16,290 --> 00:07:17,390
Come on, son.

56
00:07:19,310 --> 00:07:20,910
My mission is very important.

57
00:07:22,010 --> 00:07:24,510
My Savcı brother needs me, Bamsı Bey.

58
00:07:27,840 --> 00:07:30,640
Abruhhaman Gazi told me about everything.

59
00:07:30,940 --> 00:07:34,240
However, my Osman, please don’t.

60
00:07:35,010 --> 00:07:39,440
So that you and your father will be on
good terms.

61
00:07:40,010 --> 00:07:41,410
Let’s go, my son.

62
00:07:43,240 --> 00:07:44,810
Send him my regards.

63
00:07:45,840 --> 00:07:48,040
I put a man on my brother’s tail.

64
00:07:48,210 --> 00:07:50,010
And I will find where he is.

65
00:07:51,140 --> 00:07:56,540
Now, I have to go against my father’s
orders.

66
00:07:57,640 --> 00:08:01,040
Finding Möngke is the only way to stop
Geyhatu.

67
00:08:02,340 --> 00:08:04,910
Even if your father tells you to stop,
son?

68
00:08:05,940 --> 00:08:08,210
I know it will have bad consequences.

69
00:08:10,010 --> 00:08:13,640
And that, nothing will be the same
between me and my father.

70
00:08:13,940 --> 00:08:18,080
However, the mad horse inside me tells
me to go on.

71
00:08:18,950 --> 00:08:20,850
It tells me to find my brother!

72
00:08:22,980 --> 00:08:26,350
Son...

73
00:08:27,780 --> 00:08:31,150
… is it really the mad horse inside you…

74
00:08:32,280 --> 00:08:34,280
… or is it your honour?

75
00:08:37,880 --> 00:08:39,780
Don’t you believe me, Bamsı Bey?

76
00:08:40,950 --> 00:08:42,850
My sturdy Osman…

77
00:08:43,580 --> 00:08:45,280
… I’m only scared.

78
00:08:45,580 --> 00:08:47,380
I’m only scared…

79
00:08:48,250 --> 00:08:51,750
… because you are walking on Al-Sirat.

80
00:08:53,250 --> 00:08:56,580
Many Valiants and Heroes…

81
00:08:56,750 --> 00:08:59,580
… we lost…

82
00:08:59,850 --> 00:09:03,680
…as the results of such games of Devil.

83
00:09:06,280 --> 00:09:11,480
The dream of becoming a hero killed many
Valiants of ours.

84
00:09:13,850 --> 00:09:19,250
So, tell me son, are you faltering in the
very same dream?

85
00:09:24,350 --> 00:09:28,880
If I ever go against my father’s words
and follow my honour…

86
00:09:28,980 --> 00:09:33,180
… I shall be reaped inside out and
chopped by swords.

87
00:09:36,880 --> 00:09:38,350
If you say so..

88
00:09:41,150 --> 00:09:42,750
… so be it then (Eiwallah).

89
00:09:42,950 --> 00:09:44,450
So be it.

90
00:09:45,850 --> 00:09:50,550
May Allah be with you, from now on.

91
00:10:08,350 --> 00:10:09,790
My Bamsı Bey.

92
00:10:10,550 --> 00:10:12,790
If I don’t make it back to Tent…

93
00:10:13,990 --> 00:10:15,390
… tell my father…

94
00:10:16,650 --> 00:10:18,290
… to give his blessings.

95
00:10:21,650 --> 00:10:23,150
Tell him to forgive me.

96
00:10:49,260 --> 00:10:51,690
You did a good job, Möngke.

97
00:10:51,760 --> 00:10:53,390
A very good job, indeed.

98
00:10:53,690 --> 00:10:55,790
You are my beloved, Möngke.

99
00:10:57,560 --> 00:10:59,490
Of course I shall be your beloved.

100
00:10:59,960 --> 00:11:04,090
I gave you Kayıs and you will give me
father’s flesh.

101
00:11:05,760 --> 00:11:08,860
You will relieve his anger by pretending
to save me.

102
00:11:08,990 --> 00:11:11,660
You will save Kayıs from a huge massacre.

103
00:11:11,660 --> 00:11:14,690
You will shine like a star before the
eyes of Turks.

104
00:11:14,890 --> 00:11:18,390
You are the one who will benefit the most
from this, Möngke.

105
00:11:18,590 --> 00:11:20,890
Your father’s grave will be at Söğüt…

106
00:11:20,990 --> 00:11:23,090
… and you will replace him.

107
00:11:25,090 --> 00:11:27,060
How are you going to kill him?

108
00:11:30,890 --> 00:11:33,410
Your conscience will hurt if I tell you
so.

109
00:11:33,910 --> 00:11:38,010
I tied a rock to my conscience and threw
into Caspian Sea.

110
00:11:38,240 --> 00:11:39,940
I tell my plans to no one.

111
00:11:40,940 --> 00:11:42,940
The ground may have ears.

112
00:11:43,040 --> 00:11:45,910
You just keep dreaming of the crown you
will take.

113
00:11:46,010 --> 00:11:51,940
Who knows, maybe you will become the Khan
of Mongols once you replace your father.

114
00:11:51,940 --> 00:11:54,010
Genghis Khan is my ancestor.

115
00:11:54,340 --> 00:11:56,610
Khanship is my birth right.

116
00:11:57,140 --> 00:11:59,240
And you are my friend for life.

117
00:12:00,310 --> 00:12:02,610
Once I establish my own state...

118
00:12:02,710 --> 00:12:05,810
… try not to be an enemy but a friend.

119
00:12:07,740 --> 00:12:10,110
I have to go now.

120
00:12:11,540 --> 00:12:15,210
In the meantime, you shall learn how
Savcı found about this place.

121
00:12:15,340 --> 00:12:17,310
And that if someone else knows too.

122
00:12:17,440 --> 00:12:22,510
Do the things I tell you so that our
heads will stay on their place.

123
00:12:29,480 --> 00:12:31,750
Fool…

124
00:12:31,850 --> 00:12:33,650
… eventually, your turn will come.

125
00:12:37,450 --> 00:12:39,180
Take them away!

126
00:12:39,350 --> 00:12:43,050
Once you kill my father, it will be your
turn.

127
00:12:54,850 --> 00:12:58,880
Brother, what if something happened to
our Bey?

128
00:13:27,750 --> 00:13:31,150
You two are Alps who act like sad owls.

129
00:13:33,150 --> 00:13:35,980
Our Bey has been away for too long,
Kumral Abdal.

130
00:13:36,150 --> 00:13:38,280
Do you like your Bey so much?

131
00:13:38,450 --> 00:13:40,150
More than our own lives.

132
00:13:42,250 --> 00:13:45,380
I would believe you if I didn’t see the
things I saw.

133
00:13:49,180 --> 00:13:51,350
Do we have flaws, Kumral Abdal?

134
00:13:51,480 --> 00:13:53,180
No human is flawless!

135
00:13:54,050 --> 00:13:55,680
It's worse than that.

136
00:13:57,080 --> 00:14:00,050
Please, we are already troubled,
Kumbral Abdal.

137
00:14:00,180 --> 00:14:02,450
Tell us already if we have any flaws.

138
00:14:02,450 --> 00:14:04,380
So that we can change for good.

139
00:14:04,680 --> 00:14:07,550
We wouldn’t like to be bashful for our
Bey.

140
00:14:07,680 --> 00:14:10,680
Your heart and your tongue act the
opposite way.

141
00:14:11,250 --> 00:14:13,850
You know what they tell about such people.

142
00:14:15,090 --> 00:14:17,950
May Allah never allow that.

143
00:14:18,050 --> 00:14:20,090
Since when we are heathens?

144
00:14:20,950 --> 00:14:24,390
There are some who say they believe…

145
00:14:24,750 --> 00:14:27,350
… but they never surrender to Allah.

146
00:14:27,390 --> 00:14:30,290
Don’t you ever become one of them.

147
00:14:34,290 --> 00:14:39,050
He who loves, never gets sad or worried.

148
00:14:39,090 --> 00:14:42,190
At once, reach to the level of those who
surrendered!

149
00:14:49,650 --> 00:14:51,590
How can we reach to that level?

150
00:14:56,890 --> 00:14:58,890
I know but I won’t tell you.

151
00:14:59,750 --> 00:15:02,190
After all, you are already in the
melting pot.

152
00:15:02,290 --> 00:15:04,290
Perhaps, you will find out yourself.

153
00:15:04,490 --> 00:15:07,460
You need to be burned and cooked
for a while.

154
00:15:13,060 --> 00:15:14,860
Hand this to your Bey.

155
00:15:20,760 --> 00:15:22,390
I will go now.

156
00:15:22,490 --> 00:15:24,360
My mission is completed.

157
00:15:25,490 --> 00:15:26,860
Kumral Abdal!

158
00:15:31,690 --> 00:15:33,560
Where are you going?

159
00:15:54,440 --> 00:15:56,610
My Rab, may you protect our reason.

160
00:15:59,840 --> 00:16:02,340
Our level is not a level at all, brother.

161
00:16:02,810 --> 00:16:06,010
If we continue like this, we may end up
in hell.

162
00:16:07,140 --> 00:16:09,140
May Allah never allow that, brother.

163
00:16:09,260 --> 00:16:10,690
May we pledge.

164
00:16:24,740 --> 00:16:26,810
Selâmün aleyküm.

165
00:16:26,840 --> 00:16:29,710
Aleyküm selam, my Bey.

166
00:16:29,840 --> 00:16:32,440
I hope you are okay, Göktuğ.

167
00:16:32,610 --> 00:16:33,940
Thanks to Allah, my Bey.

168
00:16:34,010 --> 00:16:35,240
Thanks to Allah.

169
00:16:36,710 --> 00:16:39,510
I’m standing here, thanks to Abdurrahman
Gazi.

170
00:16:47,280 --> 00:16:48,950
I knew it.

171
00:16:50,880 --> 00:16:52,480
I knew it!

172
00:16:56,050 --> 00:16:57,550
My Valiant father.

173
00:16:57,950 --> 00:16:59,280
My lifeblood father.

174
00:17:13,950 --> 00:17:16,280
Kumral Abdal gave this, my Bey.

175
00:17:33,850 --> 00:17:35,380
What’s that, my Bey?

176
00:17:35,480 --> 00:17:37,750
Our guide to Devil’s pit.

177
00:17:40,380 --> 00:17:42,150
Let’s go.

178
00:17:42,180 --> 00:17:44,350
My brother is waiting for us.

179
00:18:13,580 --> 00:18:15,350
I hope it's for the good.

180
00:18:15,480 --> 00:18:18,150
You are taking away your goods from
the shelf.

181
00:18:18,150 --> 00:18:19,880
What else can I do, Davut brother?

182
00:18:19,950 --> 00:18:22,150
Our Tent is not the same as it was.

183
00:18:22,180 --> 00:18:24,580
We didn’t even make the first sale of
the day.

184
00:18:24,750 --> 00:18:26,890
I will try my luck somewhere else.

185
00:18:27,750 --> 00:18:28,950
Patience.

186
00:18:28,990 --> 00:18:31,190
We are going through hard days.

187
00:18:31,490 --> 00:18:33,750
You can’t surrender like this.

188
00:18:34,050 --> 00:18:36,750
We are always struggling with something.

189
00:18:36,890 --> 00:18:38,890
When will we able to feed ourselves?

190
00:18:39,050 --> 00:18:40,890
Where are you thinking of going?

191
00:18:40,950 --> 00:18:42,250
No idea, Davut brother.

192
00:18:43,990 --> 00:18:47,550
They say, there is business in Yalvak
Arslan’s Tent.

193
00:18:47,590 --> 00:18:49,150
I will try there.

194
00:18:49,150 --> 00:18:50,450
You coward!

195
00:18:51,550 --> 00:18:54,090
You are running away because of hardships!

196
00:18:54,350 --> 00:18:55,850
Look at me!

197
00:18:55,890 --> 00:18:58,550
You can’t achieve anything without
struggling!

198
00:18:58,690 --> 00:19:03,150
If you ever try to run away, I’ll burn
you alive!

199
00:19:03,350 --> 00:19:05,050
Okay, I get it, Davut Brother.

200
00:19:05,190 --> 00:19:08,250
Is your strength only enough for wretched
ones like me?

201
00:19:10,550 --> 00:19:13,090
You only want to choose the easy way.

202
00:19:13,250 --> 00:19:14,790
Don’t.

203
00:19:16,190 --> 00:19:19,490
Now, put the goods back on the shelf.

204
00:20:00,510 --> 00:20:02,340
I’m ready to die for you.

205
00:20:02,340 --> 00:20:03,910
Thank you, blacksmith!

206
00:20:04,110 --> 00:20:06,000
Welcome!

207
00:20:10,740 --> 00:20:12,650
Welcome, my Bey.

208
00:20:12,800 --> 00:20:14,240
Thank you.

209
00:20:31,840 --> 00:20:36,240
Know that I won’t greet anyone before I
greet my Bey.

210
00:20:36,310 --> 00:20:37,810
He is inside, my Bey.

211
00:20:45,510 --> 00:20:49,150
Do I have your excuse, my Bey?

212
00:20:54,140 --> 00:20:55,310
Come in.

213
00:21:28,680 --> 00:21:30,750
Where does the path lead?

214
00:21:32,480 --> 00:21:34,150
To the Red Apple.

215
00:21:35,480 --> 00:21:37,090
For what cause?

216
00:21:38,350 --> 00:21:42,280
For Shahada.

217
00:21:44,180 --> 00:21:47,350
Oh, look at my mighty Valiant!

218
00:21:47,450 --> 00:21:48,780
My Bey!

219
00:22:00,150 --> 00:22:03,750
My dear Bey!

220
00:22:03,880 --> 00:22:06,980
I’ve been waiting for this moment for
too long.

221
00:22:07,080 --> 00:22:10,950
Now that these eyes are on your presence…

222
00:22:11,050 --> 00:22:17,050
… may my Rab, take my remaining years and
give them to you.

223
00:22:21,380 --> 00:22:24,550
May my Rab never separate us, even in
the after life.

224
00:22:24,680 --> 00:22:26,250
Amin.

225
00:22:26,480 --> 00:22:28,680
-Amin.
-With Allah's permission.

226
00:22:31,780 --> 00:22:34,780
Okay…

227
00:22:34,950 --> 00:22:36,780
… your Bamsı Beyrek is all good.

228
00:22:36,850 --> 00:22:39,050
He is very good indeed.

229
00:22:44,350 --> 00:22:46,850
What’s the situation with escrows?

230
00:22:48,390 --> 00:22:50,990
Anything…

231
00:22:51,290 --> 00:22:53,550
… everything is under control.

232
00:22:53,690 --> 00:22:55,990
Don't you worry, my Bey.

233
00:22:56,750 --> 00:23:01,590
When the time comes, everything will be
revealed.

234
00:23:03,790 --> 00:23:08,350
Then, with Allah’s permission, the sun
will rise again.

235
00:23:09,150 --> 00:23:12,450
Our state will stand straight once again.

236
00:23:13,890 --> 00:23:17,290
With Allah’s permission, my Bey.

237
00:23:30,260 --> 00:23:32,290
Tell me, Bamsı.

238
00:23:38,050 --> 00:23:39,660
Don’t tire out yourself.

239
00:23:48,190 --> 00:23:49,790
I know my Bey.

240
00:23:50,590 --> 00:23:53,560
I know where your Osman is.

241
00:23:55,060 --> 00:23:56,590
So do I.

242
00:24:01,690 --> 00:24:04,260
He told me he has a man on Savcı’s tail.

243
00:24:04,590 --> 00:24:06,460
He knows where he is.

244
00:24:07,060 --> 00:24:10,860
He says he won’t come back to Tent unless
he finds his brother.

245
00:24:23,440 --> 00:24:25,910
My Bey...

246
00:24:28,010 --> 00:24:31,940
... didn’t he do the right thing by
following his brother?

247
00:24:32,440 --> 00:24:34,340
Let me be your sacrifice.

248
00:24:34,910 --> 00:24:37,540
At least, you tell me something about it.

249
00:24:37,710 --> 00:24:41,540
He may pretty much support his Savcı
brother.

250
00:24:45,518 --> 00:24:47,068
He didn't listen to my words.

251
00:24:48,164 --> 00:24:51,314
I grabbed his hand and took him to
the Tent...

252
00:24:52,624 --> 00:24:54,514
... yet again he didn't listen.

253
00:24:59,114 --> 00:25:02,844
He doesn't listen to his father's,
his Bey's words.

254
00:25:05,964 --> 00:25:10,804
Then what is necessary
has to be done!

255
00:25:49,840 --> 00:25:57,360
It’s time to make harsh
decisions about Osman.

256
00:26:00,720 --> 00:26:07,520
If he’s like this while I’m alive,
I don’t know what he’ll do…

257
00:26:07,520 --> 00:26:11,480
… to follow what he thinks is the truth.

258
00:26:13,840 --> 00:26:19,920
My Bey. Osman went too far. I know.

259
00:26:20,200 --> 00:26:23,320
But he has good intentions.

260
00:26:25,040 --> 00:26:30,040
The road to hell is filled with
stones of kindness.

261
00:26:34,680 --> 00:26:39,960
What would you do if you were
worried about Gündoğdu Bey?

262
00:26:39,960 --> 00:26:44,640
You also know that my
Osman loves his brothers.

263
00:26:44,640 --> 00:26:50,640
He went because he loves his brother.
Not because he wants to disobey you.

264
00:26:51,000 --> 00:26:55,480
Osman is just one of my Beys.

265
00:26:56,200 --> 00:27:03,520
If every one of my Beys follows their own
truth, what will this Tent’s future be?

266
00:27:04,800 --> 00:27:11,880
Do you ever think of that? We’ll
put the tent in order immediately.

267
00:27:13,480 --> 00:27:19,360
- I’m here for your orders, my Bey.
- Thank you.

268
00:27:20,800 --> 00:27:26,840
We’ll build a defence line.
The sands are running out.

269
00:27:26,840 --> 00:27:31,200
We don’t know what
that dog Geyhatu will do.

270
00:27:33,280 --> 00:27:37,240
You’re in charge of the defence line.

271
00:27:37,240 --> 00:27:39,560
Start the preparations.

272
00:27:40,920 --> 00:27:44,000
Thank you, my Bey!

273
00:28:59,440 --> 00:29:02,720
Why are you smiling?
Are you pleased with yourself?

274
00:29:02,720 --> 00:29:07,360
- I understand the situation now.
- What is it?

275
00:29:07,520 --> 00:29:11,680
You blamed Osman and made your escape.

276
00:29:12,520 --> 00:29:15,160
How did you find where I was hiding?

277
00:29:16,120 --> 00:29:18,920
What is such a trick’s intention anyway?

278
00:29:20,600 --> 00:29:24,000
What were you expecting to happen
after you blamed Osman?

279
00:29:27,480 --> 00:29:34,280
Your father would be angry and
come to Söğüt with his army.

280
00:29:35,480 --> 00:29:38,320
How did you find this place, I asked!

281
00:29:38,640 --> 00:29:44,720
Okay. How do you benefit from this?

282
00:29:45,040 --> 00:29:49,000
Answer my question? How did you trace me?

283
00:29:49,000 --> 00:29:51,000
Does anyone else know?

284
00:29:53,720 --> 00:29:56,680
Are you afraid your father
will hear about it, Möngke?

285
00:30:00,720 --> 00:30:04,200
You’re afraid of your father
as much as you hate him, correct?

286
00:30:12,400 --> 00:30:16,120
Someone is going to kill
your father in Söğüt, correct?

287
00:30:25,080 --> 00:30:30,120
You were going to get your father
killed and blame Osman for it, correct?

288
00:31:02,680 --> 00:31:04,880
How did you find this place? Talk!

289
00:31:06,360 --> 00:31:11,280
You’re a smart man. You know
what will happen if you don’t talk.

290
00:31:12,560 --> 00:31:18,840
You will kill me whether I talk or not.

291
00:31:19,200 --> 00:31:22,760
But I have one with before I die.

292
00:31:23,480 --> 00:31:27,360
Give me the name of that
dog who collaborated with you.

293
00:31:41,440 --> 00:31:46,160
Tie him up to the bone breaker.
His death will be painful.

294
00:31:49,800 --> 00:31:53,920
I’m sick of this place anyways.
And I’m not in a hurry.

295
00:32:18,440 --> 00:32:20,720
You’re all in the herbs again, Lena.

296
00:32:20,960 --> 00:32:23,840
Thank you. Habits of my mother.

297
00:32:26,320 --> 00:32:28,520
It’s my first time seeing this one.

298
00:32:28,520 --> 00:32:32,200
It’s a cure for everything.
I’ll make a new medicine from it.

299
00:32:34,440 --> 00:32:38,480
And maybe it will help you have a child.

300
00:32:38,480 --> 00:32:41,920
Do you think it will be?

301
00:32:41,920 --> 00:32:43,840
Of course it will!

302
00:32:43,840 --> 00:32:47,680
Every herb has a language. If you can
figure it out, you’ll get its benefits.

303
00:32:49,040 --> 00:32:50,520
Inshallah!

304
00:32:51,360 --> 00:32:53,760
Any news from Osman Bey lately?

305
00:32:54,200 --> 00:32:58,720
He set off with his horse after
hearing what happened to Göktuğ.

306
00:33:00,080 --> 00:33:03,960
Ertuğrul Bey won’t allow something
to happen to Göktuğ. Don’t worry.

307
00:33:03,960 --> 00:33:06,560
Osman Bey also knows this.

308
00:33:07,600 --> 00:33:11,600
Yes. But that tyrant called Vladius
won’t let go of the situation.

309
00:33:16,720 --> 00:33:19,600
Have you heard of this name?

310
00:33:35,600 --> 00:33:37,560
Hazal Hatun!

311
00:33:41,560 --> 00:33:42,600
What’s the situation?

312
00:33:42,600 --> 00:33:45,280
I found it while cleaning
Ertuğrul Bey’s tent.

313
00:34:24,239 --> 00:34:30,800
So, the old bird will soon fly away.

314
00:34:33,600 --> 00:34:36,400
Be ready, brother!

315
00:34:43,000 --> 00:34:46,800
I hope Osman Bey and Savcı Bey
will return safe and sound.

316
00:34:47,400 --> 00:34:51,320
I hope Osman Bey didn’t
disobey his father.

317
00:34:57,760 --> 00:35:02,960
Hatuns! Have you heard of what happened?

318
00:35:02,960 --> 00:35:04,480
What is it, Hazal Hatun?

319
00:35:04,480 --> 00:35:09,120
Did you hear something?
Or did Bamsı Bey bring any news?

320
00:35:09,800 --> 00:35:13,560
Göktuğ escaped the dungeon.

321
00:35:13,560 --> 00:35:15,400
What are you saying, Hazal Hatun?

322
00:35:16,240 --> 00:35:20,640
Everyone’s saying that Osman did it.

323
00:35:22,400 --> 00:35:26,520
As if all of our troubles
weren’t enough, now this!

324
00:35:26,520 --> 00:35:29,360
Osman Bey doesn’t disobey
his father, Hazal Hatun!

325
00:35:29,360 --> 00:35:31,640
Something fishy is going on.

326
00:35:32,400 --> 00:35:38,440
My Bala! Everything is obvious.
Besides, there’s more.

327
00:35:38,440 --> 00:35:42,960
Osman Bey disappeared with his alp Boran.

328
00:35:46,320 --> 00:35:51,760
So, Bala Hatun? You couldn’t
get a hold of your man.

329
00:35:51,760 --> 00:35:53,640
What will happen now?

330
00:35:53,640 --> 00:35:59,680
Ertuğrul Bey is dealing with Osman’s
madness in the middle of everything!

331
00:36:00,280 --> 00:36:02,240
Enough, Hazal Hatun!

332
00:36:03,600 --> 00:36:07,480
If Osman Bey is doing something,
he has a reason for it!

333
00:36:11,320 --> 00:36:16,120
Bala! I warned you countless
times as your elder!

334
00:36:16,120 --> 00:36:20,440
A Hatun disciplines her man, I said.

335
00:36:20,440 --> 00:36:30,200
But instead of disciplining your man,
you’re attacking us with your words!

336
00:36:30,200 --> 00:36:36,000
I trusted and believed you. But I see
that the devil captured your heart!

337
00:36:36,000 --> 00:36:38,200
And your tongue became the devil’s tongue!

338
00:36:39,680 --> 00:36:43,440
Bala! Do something about your words or--

339
00:36:43,440 --> 00:36:44,880
Or what?!

340
00:36:46,600 --> 00:36:49,400
Or I know how to tear it off.

341
00:36:50,040 --> 00:36:54,120
Try it if you’re brave enough!
See what happens to you!

342
00:37:01,440 --> 00:37:08,880
I called you my bride, my daughter.
You fell from my grace, Bala.

343
00:37:09,800 --> 00:37:17,240
You’ll learn what that means
but it will be too late.

344
00:37:48,280 --> 00:37:52,920
My Bey! Their lair Kumral Abdal was
talking about must be this way!

345
00:37:52,920 --> 00:37:55,160
Then we will destroy that lair!

346
00:37:55,160 --> 00:37:57,560
- Will we infiltrate it, my Bey?
- We will hit it.

347
00:37:57,560 --> 00:38:02,280
We’ll destroy everything! Let’s go!

348
00:38:13,800 --> 00:38:16,760
Bala Hatun won’t be able
to give Osman Bey a child!

349
00:38:16,760 --> 00:38:21,000
Pity! How can a man like
Osman Bey be without a child?

350
00:38:21,000 --> 00:38:23,360
They’re a looking for a new Hatun for him.

351
00:38:23,360 --> 00:38:26,280
I wouldn’t wish it on my worst enemy!

352
00:38:26,280 --> 00:38:30,280
How can Osman Bey be without a child?

353
00:38:36,360 --> 00:38:40,720
Hatuns! They’re looking
for a Hatun for Osman Bey.

354
00:38:40,720 --> 00:38:43,400
Since Bala Hatun can’t have children!

355
00:38:43,400 --> 00:38:46,440
It’s the right thing! Osman
Bey is our Tent’s future!

356
00:38:46,440 --> 00:38:49,520
If he doesn’t have children,
he won’t be sitting on that throne!

357
00:38:49,960 --> 00:38:51,960
And Lena Hatun is pregnant again.

358
00:38:53,520 --> 00:38:55,400
Excuse me.

359
00:39:07,360 --> 00:39:12,400
You’ll see what it means
to threaten me, Bala.

360
00:39:14,640 --> 00:39:19,000
This Tent will be your hell.

361
00:39:36,000 --> 00:39:40,480
You look sad, Bala.

362
00:39:42,920 --> 00:39:46,560
How can I not be? Everything’s on fire.

363
00:39:47,760 --> 00:39:50,640
As if dealing with
our enemies wasn’t enough.

364
00:39:50,640 --> 00:39:52,960
We’re dealing with the devils among us.

365
00:39:55,240 --> 00:39:57,240
Hazal Hatun again?

366
00:39:58,440 --> 00:40:00,800
I thought she was innocent.

367
00:40:01,760 --> 00:40:05,360
She’s trying to cause chaos
by breaking my bond with Lena Hatun.

368
00:40:05,800 --> 00:40:08,680
She came to this Tent for a reason, Gonca.

369
00:40:09,520 --> 00:40:13,320
There’s definitely a reason. We will see.

370
00:40:15,640 --> 00:40:17,600
May Allah protect us.

371
00:40:23,240 --> 00:40:26,600
- Good luck, Hatuns!
- Thank you.

372
00:40:31,160 --> 00:40:36,080
Bala Hatun. We’ve heard that
Osman Bey was looking for a new Hatun.

373
00:40:39,000 --> 00:40:41,200
Why would that be, Hatun?

374
00:40:41,200 --> 00:40:43,080
Because you couldn’t get pregnant.

375
00:40:46,440 --> 00:40:51,520
Take care of yourself. There’s a doctor
in Sivrihisar. You should see him.

376
00:41:24,960 --> 00:41:28,280
Everyone knows about it now, my lady.

377
00:41:28,280 --> 00:41:31,360
Good job, my beautiful daughter.

378
00:41:34,560 --> 00:41:37,680
She made everyone talk about me.

379
00:41:42,000 --> 00:41:48,560
Osman will also hear about it.
He will be embarrassed because of me.

380
00:41:55,080 --> 00:42:03,560
Bala! Don’t give up that easily!
We’ll find a way.

381
00:42:03,560 --> 00:42:11,640
It doesn’t matter, Gonca!
I’m thinking about Osman. He has dreams.

382
00:42:11,640 --> 00:42:15,600
I don’t want those dreams
to be dreams because of me.

383
00:42:15,600 --> 00:42:19,800
My Bala! What can you do
other than look for solutions?

384
00:42:22,000 --> 00:42:24,120
I’ll sacrifice myself for Osman Bey.

385
00:42:24,120 --> 00:42:29,560
What those that even mean, Bala?
Don’t say that!

386
00:42:29,560 --> 00:42:32,600
We give our lives up for
other’s lives, Gonca!

387
00:42:35,000 --> 00:42:40,160
Osman is this Tent’s hope.
Every Turkman’s hope.

388
00:42:42,687 --> 00:42:44,406
...to keep that hope alive...

389
00:42:47,035 --> 00:42:50,846
...I can even
marry Osman myself.

390
00:44:48,854 --> 00:44:52,083
We have little more to go, my bey.
The preparations are done.

391
00:44:55,859 --> 00:45:01,193
-Then, may Allah bless our holy war.
-My bey, what if we return empty-handed?

392
00:45:01,642 --> 00:45:04,132
What if Savcı Bey had solved everything?

393
00:45:04,132 --> 00:45:09,388
It's possible. But something inside me
don't let me wait.

394
00:45:12,054 --> 00:45:13,949
Let's set off.

395
00:46:20,507 --> 00:46:23,888
What will happen when you replace
your father?

396
00:46:24,862 --> 00:46:28,651
So, you finally came round.
What will happen?

397
00:46:32,940 --> 00:46:36,129
Will you kill Argun Khan like you
will kill your father?

398
00:46:36,412 --> 00:46:39,618
My father will do it for me.

399
00:46:40,776 --> 00:46:44,236
Well, well. What a loving family.

400
00:46:49,477 --> 00:46:53,256
So, you will be the Mongol Khagan?

401
00:46:54,185 --> 00:46:57,982
You will get everything without deserving.

402
00:47:19,303 --> 00:47:28,330
Now, you better start speaking. Your suffering
will end. You will get a swift and sweet death.

403
00:47:36,959 --> 00:47:40,463
I won't give you this pleasure.

404
00:47:46,565 --> 00:47:49,276
We'll see.

405
00:48:08,803 --> 00:48:12,729
A bear-like man came out of the forest,
Nicola. He took Osman.

406
00:48:13,833 --> 00:48:15,625
Say that again.

407
00:48:15,834 --> 00:48:19,724
Just when we hunted Osman, a bear
got him from us.

408
00:48:19,724 --> 00:48:24,700
Tell me that again. Tell me that again!
Again!

409
00:48:26,965 --> 00:48:31,058
A bear saved Osman.

410
00:48:31,058 --> 00:48:38,074
A bear? A bear! A bear!

411
00:48:39,968 --> 00:48:45,516
And you? Couldn't you show them
who the real bear is?

412
00:48:49,645 --> 00:48:54,254
I want to drink blood, not wine.
Blood! Blood!

413
00:49:03,143 --> 00:49:10,873
I will get such revenge from Ertuğrul that
I'll rip his heart. His heart!

414
00:49:12,113 --> 00:49:15,504
Let's make them puke blood, Nicola.

415
00:49:29,162 --> 00:49:31,759
What's in your mind, Nicola?

416
00:49:32,884 --> 00:49:37,950
We'll go after Ertuğrul's other son,
like a nightmare.

417
00:49:38,497 --> 00:49:40,451
A nightmare.

418
00:49:55,465 --> 00:49:57,843
Ertuğrul...

419
00:50:06,920 --> 00:50:09,851
There will be ditches dug on the
entrances of the fort.

420
00:50:10,061 --> 00:50:13,067
And you will build steel stakes for
those traps.

421
00:50:13,072 --> 00:50:14,895
This should be done before night.

422
00:50:14,895 --> 00:50:16,735
Are we in that much danger, my bey?

423
00:50:17,340 --> 00:50:21,993
We think that Nikola will attack by
taking the opportunity

424
00:50:22,461 --> 00:50:27,261
I want you to take the best Alps and
masons with you...

425
00:50:27,299 --> 00:50:29,565
...and close every hole you find
on the walls.

426
00:50:29,565 --> 00:50:30,735
As you command, my bey.

427
00:50:30,735 --> 00:50:33,772
I want the locks of the storehouses to
be changed too.

428
00:50:33,772 --> 00:50:36,162
We can even change the doors
if you want, my bey.

429
00:50:36,243 --> 00:50:39,813
Good. Now I'm going to take the taxes to Söğüt.

430
00:50:39,818 --> 00:50:42,768
This will all be done before I return,
all right?

431
00:50:42,768 --> 00:50:44,259
All right, my bey.

432
00:50:59,553 --> 00:51:01,929
Mashallah, mashallah.

433
00:51:02,474 --> 00:51:05,004
Thank Allah, this year was plentiful.

434
00:51:06,923 --> 00:51:09,497
Come on Alps, Come on.

435
00:51:48,139 --> 00:51:49,909
Intruders!

436
00:51:50,550 --> 00:51:52,790
Intruders!

437
00:52:03,730 --> 00:52:06,085
Osman...

438
00:52:11,474 --> 00:52:14,193
How did he find here?

439
00:52:15,421 --> 00:52:17,982
Your death has come, Möngke.

440
00:52:27,091 --> 00:52:29,353
Go and check them out.

441
00:53:31,450 --> 00:53:34,865
Welcome, my bey. Welcome, my bey.

442
00:53:38,155 --> 00:53:41,692
Welcome, welcome, my bey.

443
00:53:43,695 --> 00:53:45,652
Gündüz Bey.

444
00:54:00,286 --> 00:54:02,098
Nikola.

445
00:54:03,405 --> 00:54:06,294
As you see, I'm unarmed.

446
00:54:18,131 --> 00:54:20,532
As my soldier that you killed.

447
00:54:25,461 --> 00:54:27,582
What do you want, Nikola?

448
00:54:40,370 --> 00:54:42,610
Justice.

449
00:55:08,894 --> 00:55:10,451
My bey!

450
00:55:17,920 --> 00:55:20,128
Gündüz Bey.

451
00:55:25,485 --> 00:55:30,028
You will pay the price of breaking
the agreement.

452
00:55:30,709 --> 00:55:39,967
Breaking it? Gündüz Bey, I came here
to get my right. An eye for an eye.

453
00:55:52,615 --> 00:55:59,278
In return of my dead soldier.
I'll take a piece from Ertuğrul.

454
00:56:46,065 --> 00:56:47,365
Brother.

455
00:57:01,092 --> 00:57:02,278
Brother.

456
00:57:23,957 --> 00:57:27,954
Brother. Brother. Brother.

457
00:57:30,173 --> 00:57:32,731
Please, open your eyes.

458
00:57:32,731 --> 00:57:36,371
-Brother. -Brother.

459
00:57:43,629 --> 00:57:46,162
-Möngke deceived us all.
-How did you get it.

460
00:57:46,162 --> 00:57:53,033
You were both prisoners.
You were beaten up good, brother.

461
00:57:54,273 --> 00:57:57,820
But he was fine.
Pretty fine.

462
00:57:59,370 --> 00:58:03,767
If I was as vigilant as you,
I wouldn't be here.

463
00:58:08,750 --> 00:58:10,886
Brother.

464
00:58:16,242 --> 00:58:20,259
Without you, we wouldn't be able
to do this.

465
00:58:20,481 --> 00:58:26,683
Without you, I wouldn't be alive. It's a
good thing that you didn't listen to me.

466
00:58:28,423 --> 00:58:30,603
But...

467
00:58:32,573 --> 00:58:36,443
...be afraid of Bala.

468
00:58:40,002 --> 00:58:42,422
I'd give my life for both of you.

469
00:58:43,923 --> 00:58:45,818
My lion brother.

470
00:58:46,764 --> 00:58:50,442
Brother, we don't have much time.

471
00:59:10,714 --> 00:59:16,377
But don't worry. You won't die.
But you will suffer.

472
00:59:17,434 --> 00:59:23,344
My unarmed soldier was killed.
You killed my unarmed soldier...

473
00:59:23,344 --> 00:59:30,774
...in front of hundred of your soldiers,
despite our agreement.

474
00:59:33,199 --> 00:59:41,618
Tell your bey, if I see Osman or Göktuğ,
I will kill them.

475
00:59:46,257 --> 00:59:54,316
He either brings them and trials them.
Or I will get things right. Tell your bey.

476
00:59:54,802 --> 01:00:03,576
I won't be the one breaking the deal.
But if you break it, I'll make you pay.

477
01:00:04,656 --> 01:00:08,006
My bey! My bey!

478
01:00:15,045 --> 01:00:20,006
Gündüz Bey, I like to make people pay.

479
01:01:10,603 --> 01:01:12,444
My bey. My bey.

480
01:01:30,211 --> 01:01:32,904
I've been waiting for this for
a long time.

481
01:01:34,106 --> 01:01:37,197
What if Savcı brings Möngke,
our holy leader?

482
01:01:37,666 --> 01:01:43,023
Then we will declare war because their
horses neigh!

483
01:01:43,578 --> 01:01:48,910
It's a small Turkmen tribe.
They aren't even worth your trouble.

484
01:01:49,921 --> 01:01:56,902
-Why is this, sir?
-I wanted him to clean my honor first...

485
01:01:57,602 --> 01:02:04,621
...but now the existence of Ertuğrul
blurs my mind.

486
01:02:08,271 --> 01:02:10,873
It disturbs me.

487
01:02:15,777 --> 01:02:19,182
Osman is a roaring lion.

488
01:02:20,802 --> 01:02:25,730
We should crush his head...
...while he is little.

489
01:03:06,838 --> 01:03:09,829
We found this spy prying on us.

490
01:03:17,270 --> 01:03:21,602
Why did you bring him to me and
not just kill?

491
01:03:25,093 --> 01:03:27,959
Your weapon can't kill me.

492
01:03:32,786 --> 01:03:38,210
Kill this man, Cerkutay.
His bones will feed dogs.

493
01:03:38,464 --> 01:03:41,505
Do it yourself if you can.

494
01:03:48,314 --> 01:03:51,639
Your weapon doesn't have
the power to kill me.

495
01:03:54,282 --> 01:03:56,743
Who the hell are you?

496
01:04:01,929 --> 01:04:03,985
I'm a madman.

497
01:04:13,477 --> 01:04:16,008
What were you looking for here?

498
01:04:21,699 --> 01:04:25,197
I lost my army, I was looking for it.

499
01:04:28,932 --> 01:04:31,785
Who is the commander of your army?

500
01:04:33,849 --> 01:04:36,827
I am. Didn't you like that?

501
01:04:37,853 --> 01:04:41,864
Where is your weapon?
Where are your soldiers?

502
01:04:44,613 --> 01:04:47,183
They'll be here soon.

503
01:04:50,468 --> 01:04:54,553
-What's the matter with you?
-I came to warn you.

504
01:04:55,387 --> 01:04:59,935
-Go on your way.
-What if I don't?

505
01:05:00,963 --> 01:05:03,940
Will you stop me?

506
01:05:07,705 --> 01:05:11,911
Then, what happened to
Ebrehe's army will happen to you.

507
01:05:12,381 --> 01:05:18,271
-Who the hell is Ebrehe?
-The tyrant who attacked the mother of cities.

508
01:05:20,135 --> 01:05:24,830
-Tell me.
-I'll tell you when the time comes.

509
01:05:25,596 --> 01:05:30,462
-Now, I'm warning you.
-Enough, you worthless.

510
01:05:31,517 --> 01:05:34,140
You are wasting my time.

511
01:05:34,847 --> 01:05:38,055
Time isn't yours!

512
01:06:33,844 --> 01:06:38,085
Birds...
Birds...

513
01:06:38,761 --> 01:06:41,308
Ahmet!

514
01:06:50,559 --> 01:06:54,019
What happened in your dream?

515
01:06:56,303 --> 01:06:58,369
That tyrant.

516
01:07:00,270 --> 01:07:04,645
-That cruel man was going to come to our tents-
-Which cruel man, Ahmed?

517
01:07:08,551 --> 01:07:10,522
Geyhatu.

518
01:07:11,701 --> 01:07:13,889
That cruel man which you call Geyhatu.

519
01:07:16,825 --> 01:07:20,814
There is wisdom in dreams, Ahmed.
Tell me what you seen.

520
01:07:24,318 --> 01:07:27,331
A man came up.

521
01:07:28,882 --> 01:07:31,292
A dervish-like man.

522
01:07:32,144 --> 01:07:35,384
With his staff in his hand.

523
01:07:38,924 --> 01:07:43,293
He stood against the cruel man,
he ruined his house.

524
01:07:45,387 --> 01:07:50,527
Birds, stones, winds...

525
01:07:50,932 --> 01:07:56,242
They couldn't even use their swords.
They were all damned.

526
01:08:02,716 --> 01:08:07,561
Inshallah your dream will come true
and we will beat the cruel.

527
01:08:08,686 --> 01:08:12,354
Osman Bey will stop him.
Don't worry.

528
01:08:12,354 --> 01:08:17,533
I know, Bala Hatun. I'm not worried.
Osman Bey is a roaring lion.

529
01:08:41,751 --> 01:08:45,435
-Dumrul, you've been a comrade.
-I'd give my life to you, my bey.

530
01:08:46,676 --> 01:08:48,293
Thank you.

531
01:08:53,976 --> 01:08:57,771
I'm glad you came, brother.
It would be terrible without you.

532
01:08:58,781 --> 01:09:03,036
Thank Allah for sending me, brother.
It was our duty.

533
01:09:05,912 --> 01:09:08,076
Your duty was not coming.

534
01:09:08,252 --> 01:09:12,844
But...
I'm glad you didn't listen to us.

535
01:09:13,424 --> 01:09:15,847
It would be terrible without you.

536
01:09:16,502 --> 01:09:20,330
Tell your inner voice, we
owe it a life.

537
01:09:21,458 --> 01:09:26,639
Are our lives truly ours, brother?

538
01:09:29,892 --> 01:09:34,514
But, for the first time, we
are in such a big scheme.

539
01:09:35,302 --> 01:09:39,227
You see, even a son is planning
behind his father.

540
01:09:42,052 --> 01:09:44,547
Who do you think is
behind this?

541
01:09:45,070 --> 01:09:50,210
Someone must be holding the leash
of this dog. He can't do it alone.

542
01:09:57,447 --> 01:10:00,003
I suspect Yavlak Arslan.

543
01:10:00,596 --> 01:10:04,338
What are you saying, brother?
This is a heavy accusation.

544
01:10:08,547 --> 01:10:14,131
If we can make him talk before
going to his father, we may find it.

545
01:10:38,594 --> 01:10:43,374
Come on, my valiants!
Come on, my valiants!

546
01:10:44,430 --> 01:10:48,706
Today is the day of honor!

547
01:10:50,347 --> 01:10:54,317
Today, there is no surrender!

548
01:10:54,921 --> 01:10:58,332
Today, there is no subjugation!

549
01:10:59,400 --> 01:11:05,964
Today, there is no conceding!

550
01:11:12,488 --> 01:11:16,663
Come on, valiants!
Be united!

551
01:11:17,325 --> 01:11:21,071
Be a roaring lion!
Mashallah!

552
01:11:22,223 --> 01:11:27,127
Mashallah, Bamsı Bey. You brought
life to our tents.

553
01:11:29,206 --> 01:11:31,462
Thank you, thank you, Dündar Bey.

554
01:11:32,022 --> 01:11:36,455
Now that I saw Ertuğrul Bey,
I'm as fresh as daisy.

555
01:11:36,891 --> 01:11:43,251
The lion inside me roared.
These wrists of mine got stronger.

556
01:11:43,551 --> 01:11:46,219
Mashallah, mashallah.

557
01:11:46,219 --> 01:11:48,840
The reinforcements must've reached
Söğüt.

558
01:11:48,840 --> 01:11:51,892
Mashallah, mashallah. Let's see.

559
01:11:54,040 --> 01:12:00,466
Come on, valiants. We take measures,
but it's upt o Allah.

560
01:12:02,086 --> 01:12:11,111
If Allah doesn't want to protect us,
great mountains can't protect us.

561
01:12:11,666 --> 01:12:18,525
But if Allah...
...if Allah wants to protect us...

562
01:12:19,578 --> 01:12:23,974
Even a spider web can be an armor
for us.

563
01:12:28,452 --> 01:12:30,365
My Allah...

564
01:12:33,495 --> 01:12:38,529
...protect us, my Allah.
-Amin.

565
01:12:39,118 --> 01:12:46,677
Protect us and our tents from
the enemy, my Allah!

566
01:12:46,677 --> 01:12:50,953
-Amin.
-Amin.

567
01:12:54,487 --> 01:12:59,574
Come on, warriors. Come on, alps.
Come on, valiants.

568
01:12:59,574 --> 01:13:01,784
Today is the day of honor.

569
01:13:01,784 --> 01:13:04,668
Come on, valiants.
Come on.

570
01:13:07,872 --> 01:13:10,497
My bey, you should take a breath.

571
01:13:12,849 --> 01:13:18,421
What is it? Did you think that I'm a
hoar like you, Abdurrahman Ghazi?

572
01:13:19,379 --> 01:13:22,835
Not at all, my bey.
I just didn't want you to get tired.

573
01:13:26,648 --> 01:13:31,701
Neither enemies nor traitors
tired me all these years.

574
01:13:33,541 --> 01:13:37,373
What tires me, what bothers me...

575
01:13:38,883 --> 01:13:41,625
...is what will happen after me.

576
01:13:42,623 --> 01:13:47,148
As the father, who will I make me heir?

577
01:13:48,686 --> 01:13:52,256
It's a great responsibility, Ghazi.
A great responsibility.

578
01:13:54,584 --> 01:13:57,858
Gündüz, Savcı and Osman.

579
01:13:58,557 --> 01:14:03,721
Three gallants of mine. Even if a single
gets sad about it...

580
01:14:04,221 --> 01:14:06,569
...I'll be sad.

581
01:14:07,122 --> 01:14:11,945
If they get hurt,
my heart will hurt.

582
01:14:14,881 --> 01:14:19,913
I might stand like that but I'm a father.

583
01:14:25,037 --> 01:14:28,538
My bey, my bey. My bey, incoming!

584
01:14:31,873 --> 01:14:35,631
Clear the way! Clear!

585
01:14:36,216 --> 01:14:39,738
-May it be good, Dündar Bey.
-May it be good.

586
01:14:58,982 --> 01:15:06,038
-Gündüz? Gündüz! Gündüz!
-Gündüz Bey!

587
01:15:06,290 --> 01:15:10,020
-Gündüz, tell me who did this to you?
-Gündüz, who did this treachery?

588
01:15:10,713 --> 01:15:16,096
Nikola ambushed us, my bey.
We have wounded alps.

589
01:15:17,565 --> 01:15:22,077
Come on, carry him to the tent.
Hold here. Hold here, valiants.

590
01:15:22,281 --> 01:15:24,481
Return to your jobs.

591
01:15:24,936 --> 01:15:30,965
-Gündüz.
-Everyone, return to your jobs.

592
01:15:30,965 --> 01:15:35,475
There is no break.
There is no crying.

593
01:15:35,475 --> 01:15:39,767
Today is the day of honor.
Everyone, return to your jobs.

594
01:15:50,534 --> 01:15:54,438
Hurry, hurry, hurry!

595
01:15:56,288 --> 01:16:01,010
Gündüz, my child.
Who did this to you?

596
01:16:02,043 --> 01:16:06,329
Nikola, father, Nikola.

597
01:16:12,939 --> 01:16:16,701
Gündüz...
Gündüz, my child.

598
01:16:31,734 --> 01:16:35,090
Father, don't worry.

599
01:16:35,559 --> 01:16:39,613
I'll cure my Gündüz brother.
Come on, Alps. Let's take him in.

600
01:16:39,726 --> 01:16:42,442
-Alps, come on!
-Come on! Come on!

601
01:16:44,106 --> 01:16:46,146
Come on!

602
01:16:55,982 --> 01:16:59,006
He is taking revenge.

603
01:17:00,624 --> 01:17:03,784
I will make him regret!

604
01:17:04,125 --> 01:17:08,395
Once we get rid of this Geyhatu trouble.

605
01:17:09,952 --> 01:17:13,122
I will make him regr...

606
01:17:15,856 --> 01:17:17,376
My Bey!

607
01:17:29,220 --> 01:17:34,440
If Kayıs can save so much gold
in this short time...

608
01:17:34,651 --> 01:17:38,781
it means that they will grow.

609
01:17:39,651 --> 01:17:44,357
Vladius, we need to get in action.

610
01:17:44,357 --> 01:17:46,697
You are right, Nikola.

611
01:17:48,018 --> 01:17:50,618
What are we going to do with gold?

612
01:17:54,522 --> 01:17:57,192
I like being generous.

613
01:17:58,505 --> 01:18:01,935
Let's give it to our people.

614
01:18:03,287 --> 01:18:08,677
So that they believe in victory more.

615
01:18:39,601 --> 01:18:42,231
Yavlak Arslan from Çobanoğulları has come.

616
01:18:42,981 --> 01:18:45,041
Let him.

617
01:19:16,237 --> 01:19:21,262
If you are planning an attack to
Kayıs and Turkmens...

618
01:19:21,262 --> 01:19:24,716
taking advantage of their action with
Geyhatu's army.

619
01:19:24,716 --> 01:19:26,086
Yavlak.

620
01:19:27,872 --> 01:19:32,572
Is Osman included in what you are talking
about?

621
01:19:33,234 --> 01:19:34,664
Osman.

622
01:19:37,942 --> 01:19:42,444
What Osman?

623
01:19:45,464 --> 01:19:47,469
Yavlak.

624
01:19:47,469 --> 01:19:51,999
Stop acting like you don't know what
he has done.

625
01:19:52,080 --> 01:19:59,750
You also know that neither you nor I
can peace as long as Osman lives.

626
01:20:12,200 --> 01:20:18,665
Finally, a wise man
in the throne of enemy.

627
01:21:03,465 --> 01:21:06,065
You couldn't protect even in my dream.

628
01:22:10,169 --> 01:22:12,976
The ground swallowed him up.

629
01:22:12,976 --> 01:22:15,626
We can't find Osman and Savcı.

630
01:22:20,296 --> 01:22:27,146
Send your men to everywhere!
Everywhere!

631
01:22:29,927 --> 01:22:32,007
Osman...

632
01:22:35,160 --> 01:22:39,600
I will bury him alive.

633
01:22:47,858 --> 01:22:52,268
Who did you collaborated with?
Talk, dog!

634
01:23:05,155 --> 01:23:07,815
You are in hurry for your death!

635
01:23:08,523 --> 01:23:12,203
Talk, you dog!
Talk!

636
01:23:19,045 --> 01:23:25,195
You can't get a word from me.
My father will bury you all alive.

637
01:23:25,317 --> 01:23:27,817
The secret has been revealed.

638
01:23:27,984 --> 01:23:30,804
The secret has been revealed.

639
01:23:51,892 --> 01:23:55,722
Tell me.

640
01:23:56,534 --> 01:23:59,686
I saw, I went, as you said.

641
01:23:59,686 --> 01:24:02,457
I am back with heavy news, son of a Bey.

642
01:24:02,457 --> 01:24:07,177
May it be good. Tell us what you have.

643
01:24:14,829 --> 01:24:20,789
Osman conquered one of our biggest castles
in his father's absence.

644
01:24:21,974 --> 01:24:26,984
He humiliated two great Mongol unities
with their commanders.

645
01:24:27,015 --> 01:24:32,405
I can't imagine what this young man would
do after his father's death.

646
01:24:33,460 --> 01:24:37,600
What do you think, Yavlak?

647
01:24:37,795 --> 01:24:43,475
Osman...
Who is Osman while Dündar is there.

648
01:24:52,164 --> 01:24:55,754
Even you don't believe in what you say.

649
01:24:56,380 --> 01:25:00,290
Osman would have ten men like Dündar
in pocket.

650
01:25:00,341 --> 01:25:05,801
Neither Dündar nor his brothers can stop
him after his father dies.

651
01:25:06,620 --> 01:25:08,810
Cool.

652
01:25:08,810 --> 01:25:11,420
What interests you?

653
01:25:14,861 --> 01:25:18,801
Osman is the biggest threat for me.

654
01:25:18,897 --> 01:25:23,647
I am the biggest threat for you, Nikola.

655
01:25:29,745 --> 01:25:34,551
If you're planning an attack to Kayıs, taking
advantage of....

656
01:25:34,551 --> 01:25:36,441
their action with Geyhatu's army.

657
01:25:36,441 --> 01:25:43,441
I swear that I will bury you in this
castle's rusty stones.

658
01:25:44,394 --> 01:25:45,874
Don't worry.

659
01:25:52,236 --> 01:25:54,486
Yavlak Arslan.

660
01:25:55,891 --> 01:26:03,041
I am not intended to bother you as long as
Osman doesn't bother me.

661
01:26:22,557 --> 01:26:26,397
- What is this?
- A gift. I like it.

662
01:26:35,801 --> 01:26:38,831
I wanted our friendship to improve.

663
01:26:49,498 --> 01:26:55,188
Nikola... you don't know about roosters
at all.

664
01:26:57,336 --> 01:27:02,826
But I liked you.
You are kind.

665
01:27:03,939 --> 01:27:06,719
I will see you again.

666
01:27:25,494 --> 01:27:28,514
Me too, Yavlak.

667
01:27:29,552 --> 01:27:31,442
Me too.

668
01:28:42,074 --> 01:28:45,564
His wounds are heavy.

669
01:28:45,914 --> 01:28:48,404
My Lord, grant us with him.

670
01:28:50,888 --> 01:28:53,708
Bala bring some more balm.

671
01:28:56,222 --> 01:28:59,332
- Bring, bring, bring.
- Take it.

672
01:29:04,307 --> 01:29:08,557
He is unconscious.
He lost so much blood.

673
01:29:08,564 --> 01:29:13,654
Gündüz Bey's arm seems really bad, Lena.
He won't be able to hold sword a while.

674
01:29:23,356 --> 01:29:26,856
Lena, what's his situation?

675
01:29:26,856 --> 01:29:28,846
He will be alright, my Bey.

676
01:29:33,191 --> 01:29:36,271
Heal him, my daughter.

677
01:29:37,283 --> 01:29:43,743
Don't worry, father. My treacle water
heal him up soon.

678
01:29:58,739 --> 01:30:02,859
Bala, let's preapre some more balm.

679
01:30:40,433 --> 01:30:46,623
I am Suleiman Shah's son Ertuğrul Ghazi.

680
01:30:46,692 --> 01:30:51,751
I swear on my flag.

681
01:30:51,751 --> 01:30:57,821
I will dig out the ones who did this
to you with my dark dagger.

682
01:30:59,099 --> 01:31:03,539
I swear on my blood.

683
01:31:04,199 --> 01:31:09,439
I will torment the ones who did this
to you like they are in hell.

684
01:31:17,136 --> 01:31:19,026
Father.

685
01:31:21,792 --> 01:31:23,622
My Father.

686
01:31:25,266 --> 01:31:27,356
You shall sleep, my Gündüz.

687
01:31:29,489 --> 01:31:31,289
My sunshine.

688
01:31:33,210 --> 01:31:35,350
My child.

689
01:31:35,350 --> 01:31:39,310
Inshaallah, you stand up
as soon as possible.

690
01:31:39,310 --> 01:31:43,103
As soon as possible, my father.
Don't worry.

691
01:31:43,103 --> 01:31:46,883
We have a valiant brother who didn't
buckle under cruelty.

692
01:32:28,357 --> 01:32:35,153
May our holy war be blessed to stop
the cruels!

693
01:32:35,153 --> 01:32:38,348
Eyvallah, my Bey.

694
01:32:38,348 --> 01:32:43,010
You have a plan, we are sticking to it.
Let's see what happens, brother.

695
01:32:43,010 --> 01:32:46,130
- Let's go now.
- Bismillah.

696
01:32:46,218 --> 01:32:48,338
Ya Allah!

697
01:33:51,385 --> 01:33:55,107
I am here to help you in your rough day,
Ertuğrul Bey.

698
01:33:55,107 --> 01:34:00,097
What is it?
Do you have an army for me, Arslan?

699
01:34:02,755 --> 01:34:10,255
- I came to stop Geyhatu.
- Only my sons can stop Geyhatu, Arslan.

700
01:34:14,354 --> 01:34:16,944
I visited Nikola.

701
01:34:17,418 --> 01:34:26,218
I warned him to not set his eyes on your
castles while Geyhatu is here.

702
01:34:28,061 --> 01:34:30,121
Cruel dog!

703
01:34:31,424 --> 01:34:33,724
He backstabbed me in my rough day!

704
01:34:34,774 --> 01:34:37,634
I will make him regret!

705
01:34:41,122 --> 01:34:49,082
I will take many lives for the blood
of Gündüz and Alps...

706
01:34:49,794 --> 01:34:51,504
My Bey...

707
01:34:53,650 --> 01:34:56,350
My Bey, my Bey...

708
01:34:56,700 --> 01:34:58,660
My Ertuğrul Bey...

709
01:35:00,058 --> 01:35:02,908
My Bey, my Bey.

710
01:35:03,162 --> 01:35:05,142
Alps!

711
01:35:40,879 --> 01:35:44,519
So, Geyhatu's son
Mongke was involved in this case.

712
01:35:44,607 --> 01:35:47,657
Osman was just a bait in this game.

713
01:35:47,660 --> 01:35:52,830
My closest Alps will save Mongke and bring
him here before Geyhatu attacks the tribe.

714
01:35:54,506 --> 01:35:57,436
You'll save Kayıs from two big trouble.

715
01:35:58,433 --> 01:36:02,602
From both Geyhatu and Osman.

716
01:36:02,602 --> 01:36:06,541
I see both of them as an obstacle against
the state I will establish.

717
01:36:06,541 --> 01:36:10,191
Geyhatu with his power, Osman with
his stubborness, they hamper me.

718
01:36:10,191 --> 01:36:14,190
But today I will get rid of both of them.

719
01:36:18,365 --> 01:36:21,095
Why don't you smile?

720
01:36:22,779 --> 01:36:31,959
Ertuğrul Bey's death is not far. Osman is
the biggest trouble, we both know that.

721
01:36:33,086 --> 01:36:39,526
But that Mongke, why is Mongke in this,
brother?

722
01:36:45,065 --> 01:36:48,676
There's still a secret that you didn't
tell me about.

723
01:36:48,676 --> 01:36:51,656
You have always been wise, my sister.

724
01:36:55,359 --> 01:37:02,669
Brother, tell me for Allah's sake, what
will Geyhatu's son Mongke get?

725
01:37:08,567 --> 01:37:10,878
Geyhatu will die today.

726
01:37:10,878 --> 01:37:14,078
His son Mongke will take his place.

727
01:37:14,647 --> 01:37:20,057
Osman will be his killer, and I will
establish the state.

728
01:37:30,087 --> 01:37:33,337
What about Osman?
What if he pops up?

729
01:37:33,430 --> 01:37:38,760
I thought everything.
I set a trap in their way.

730
01:39:26,195 --> 01:39:30,235
- Let's see what happens.
- The Auburn Abdal did a good work.

731
01:39:34,519 --> 01:39:37,679
They will be in the dark jungle.

732
01:39:42,157 --> 01:39:43,747
Brothers.

733
01:39:50,091 --> 01:39:52,741
The mission is yours.

734
01:40:05,501 --> 01:40:12,681
I don't know who is in behind this, but
it will be revealed when this is over.

735
01:40:14,083 --> 01:40:17,993
Let's go, valiants. Don't waste time.

736
01:40:54,401 --> 01:40:57,851
His fever is going up, bring cold water.

737
01:41:08,807 --> 01:41:12,466
Don't be hopeless.

738
01:41:12,466 --> 01:41:17,266
Geyhatu can arrive anytime.

739
01:41:17,551 --> 01:41:21,518
We are always prepared.

740
01:41:21,518 --> 01:41:26,368
Just because our Bey is lying back there,
we won't be oppressed.

741
01:41:30,454 --> 01:41:37,074
We won't let anyone dirty our honor.

742
01:41:38,581 --> 01:41:41,711
Talk, Dündar Bey.

743
01:41:50,298 --> 01:41:54,888
Everyone gathered, they are worried about
our Bey's condition.

744
01:41:58,823 --> 01:42:02,851
As his brother, this is your mission.

745
01:42:02,851 --> 01:42:08,691
People are worried about their life
and their Bey. Console them.

746
01:43:08,307 --> 01:43:17,017
Kayı's vailant Hatuns, valiant Men,
valiant children!

747
01:43:19,771 --> 01:43:24,391
I know you love for Ertuğrul Bey, and
I also know that...

748
01:43:24,409 --> 01:43:28,909
you are in a deep sorrow.

749
01:43:29,576 --> 01:43:31,556
However, it is true.

750
01:43:33,170 --> 01:43:37,520
Our Bey's disease reappeared.

751
01:43:52,357 --> 01:43:55,427
My Allah, don't let us be rudderless.

752
01:44:02,464 --> 01:44:05,024
Our Bey will be healthy
soon, Inshaallah...

753
01:44:05,359 --> 01:44:08,339
with Allah's permission.

754
01:44:09,739 --> 01:44:14,229
Inshaallah!

755
01:44:15,827 --> 01:44:19,827
Now, you should worry about
our tribe's future...

756
01:44:20,389 --> 01:44:22,939
not his health.

757
01:44:25,964 --> 01:44:26,984
Mongols...

758
01:44:27,658 --> 01:44:29,208
are about to come.

759
01:44:29,703 --> 01:44:33,703
You're all armed, all of you.

760
01:44:34,706 --> 01:44:38,706
When the war is this close, we
should all be like...

761
01:44:39,238 --> 01:44:41,218
Ertuğrul Bey.

762
01:44:44,921 --> 01:44:48,921
Each of you will become Ertuğrul Bey.

763
01:44:49,057 --> 01:44:53,287
So that we can deserve...

764
01:44:53,759 --> 01:44:57,059
this beautiful land.

765
01:45:00,055 --> 01:45:02,985
It doesn't matter who the enemy is..

766
01:45:03,490 --> 01:45:07,490
what we should do is...

767
01:45:07,490 --> 01:45:10,270
to follow our Bey!

768
01:45:12,204 --> 01:45:16,444
Allahu Akbar! (Allah is the greatest.)
Allahu Akbar! (Allah is the greatest.)

769
01:45:16,509 --> 01:45:35,239
Allahu Akbar! (Allah is the greatest.)
Allahu Akbar! (Allah is the greatest.)

770
01:45:54,695 --> 01:45:57,835
My Bey, Geyhatu is here.

771
01:46:26,710 --> 01:46:30,090
Come on!
Everyone, go fight!

772
01:46:30,201 --> 01:46:32,571
Do your duty, come on.

773
01:47:08,280 --> 01:47:11,280
Are there any news from
Kulucahisar and Karacahisar?

774
01:47:24,940 --> 01:47:26,560
What's new?

775
01:47:27,318 --> 01:47:28,088
Nikola.

776
01:47:29,699 --> 01:47:34,069
Geyhatu is in Kızıltepe with his army.

777
01:47:35,627 --> 01:47:36,567
Good.

778
01:47:36,687 --> 01:47:37,937
What about our castles?

779
01:47:38,736 --> 01:47:42,526
Our spies are waiting for your order to
take action in both of the castles.

780
01:47:42,835 --> 01:47:44,195
I like action.

781
01:47:44,370 --> 01:47:48,370
When Ertuğrul's men and
Geyhatu's army start to fight...

782
01:47:48,467 --> 01:47:51,137
we'll go into action from three areas.

783
01:47:51,213 --> 01:47:53,343
Commander, you go Kulucahisar.

784
01:47:53,476 --> 01:47:57,036
Commander Nikis, you go Karacahisar and
you'll attack at the same time.

785
01:47:57,737 --> 01:48:01,737
And I'll support you with my own unity.

786
01:48:03,394 --> 01:48:04,424
What about Geyhatu?

787
01:48:04,552 --> 01:48:07,522
The Mongols are the real owners of
Ertuğrul's lands.

788
01:48:07,522 --> 01:48:09,742
How will we prevent Geyhatu's reaction?

789
01:48:09,778 --> 01:48:12,128
When Geyhatu takes action with his army..

790
01:48:12,128 --> 01:48:15,688
the only place that Turks can go is
Byzantine lands.

791
01:48:16,031 --> 01:48:17,511
Commander Nikis.

792
01:48:18,236 --> 01:48:22,236
Vladius will kill who runs away.

793
01:48:25,027 --> 01:48:26,767
I'm sure Geyhatu...

794
01:48:28,761 --> 01:48:30,321
will be grateful.

795
01:48:30,488 --> 01:48:32,528
What about Yavlak Arslan?

796
01:48:33,456 --> 01:48:35,256
Yavlak Arslan.

797
01:48:36,261 --> 01:48:37,951
If he attacks...

798
01:48:38,112 --> 01:48:40,102
killing him is...

799
01:48:41,800 --> 01:48:43,370
my job.

800
01:48:44,495 --> 01:48:46,055
As Caesar said...

801
01:48:47,940 --> 01:48:48,950
"I came."

802
01:48:51,403 --> 01:48:53,043
"I saw!"

803
01:48:56,040 --> 01:48:57,580
"I conquered!"

804
01:48:57,819 --> 01:49:00,229
"I came; I saw; I conquered!"

805
01:49:00,859 --> 01:49:04,859
"I came; I saw; I conquered!"

806
01:49:49,252 --> 01:49:51,062
What will we do now?

807
01:49:51,191 --> 01:49:53,881
The Mongol army.
How will we handle them?

808
01:49:53,981 --> 01:49:56,101
We'll fight, İdris Efendi.

809
01:49:58,470 --> 01:50:02,830
If we die, we die with honor.

810
01:50:30,428 --> 01:50:32,198
That's good news.

811
01:50:33,864 --> 01:50:35,414
What does it mean, my Bey?

812
01:50:36,456 --> 01:50:40,456
Geyhatu wants to talk before the fight.

813
01:50:40,586 --> 01:50:42,976
He obviously wants his son.

814
01:50:43,864 --> 01:50:46,354
We don't know about his son.

815
01:50:46,630 --> 01:50:49,150
We don't even have his dead body...

816
01:50:49,398 --> 01:50:51,468
what are you saying?

817
01:50:51,608 --> 01:50:55,608
I'll talk to him one last time.
Whatever happens.

818
01:50:55,712 --> 01:50:59,712
Arslan Bey, you're not the
Bey of our tribe.

819
01:50:59,814 --> 01:51:04,074
- This is our job.
- I'm not the Bey of the tribe, yes...

820
01:51:04,571 --> 01:51:07,441
but I'm the Bey of Beys of this land.

821
01:51:07,652 --> 01:51:09,802
Know your place, Bamsı Bey.

822
01:51:21,787 --> 01:51:24,707
No need to talk.

823
01:51:25,003 --> 01:51:28,543
Geyhatu wreaks his anger on us when
he doesn't see his son.

824
01:51:30,089 --> 01:51:31,419
Arslan Bey is right.

825
01:51:31,504 --> 01:51:35,504
We need to have time
until Savcı and Osman come.

826
01:51:36,213 --> 01:51:37,473
Then...

827
01:51:38,971 --> 01:51:42,971
the words are over and weapons will talk.

828
01:53:38,101 --> 01:53:41,591
What are you doing here, Yavlak Arslan?

829
01:53:42,799 --> 01:53:47,539
I want to talk about the problem
without having a fight.

830
01:53:48,053 --> 01:53:51,593
It's none of your business, Yavlak Arslan.

831
01:53:52,765 --> 01:53:54,885
I don't have time to talk.

832
01:53:57,383 --> 01:53:59,673
I came here to take my son back...

833
01:54:00,114 --> 01:54:01,934
and if I don't...

834
01:54:03,008 --> 01:54:07,158
I'll kill Kayıs.

835
01:54:47,973 --> 01:54:48,883
Helen.

836
01:54:50,792 --> 01:54:54,792
Take this and go to the kitchen.
I'll come after you

837
01:55:09,794 --> 01:55:10,694
Father.

838
01:55:10,846 --> 01:55:13,526
Helen is here.

839
01:55:14,477 --> 01:55:16,517
I need to learn where she is going.

840
01:55:28,059 --> 01:55:32,059
Our spies are waiting for your order to
take action in both of the castles.

841
01:55:32,217 --> 01:55:36,217
I like action. When Ertuğrul's men and
Geyhatu's army start to fight...

842
01:55:36,217 --> 01:55:40,257
we'll go into action from three areas.

843
01:56:01,254 --> 01:56:03,714
In and outs to the castle are banned.

844
01:56:03,897 --> 01:56:06,917
The bazaar will be closed.
Go back to your work.

845
01:56:23,063 --> 01:56:26,423
It'll happen during the change of shifts.

846
01:56:28,023 --> 01:56:31,013
We have to be sure about
how many are they, Nikola.

847
01:56:43,608 --> 01:56:45,318
Helen.

848
01:56:45,918 --> 01:56:48,118
You came just on time.

849
01:56:49,510 --> 01:56:52,040
Why is that privacy?

850
01:56:54,120 --> 01:56:56,360
There's a spy in our castle.

851
01:56:57,807 --> 01:57:00,977
He told where our
ammunition is to the Kayıs before.

852
01:57:01,932 --> 01:57:03,402
Until we find him and...

853
01:57:03,583 --> 01:57:07,583
hang him by the neck
on the edge of the walls...

854
01:57:08,029 --> 01:57:09,759
we need to be careful.

855
01:57:12,158 --> 01:57:16,348
Savcı, he is as troubled as Osman.

856
01:57:17,135 --> 01:57:20,525
Helen, what is going on in Kulucahisar?

857
01:57:23,647 --> 01:57:27,647
Here are the places for the watch.
There are twenty Alps on the walls.

858
01:57:28,306 --> 01:57:31,186
They're changing shifts three
times during the day.

859
01:57:35,084 --> 01:57:37,634
Are all the archers informed?

860
01:57:54,402 --> 01:57:56,072
As you ordered...

861
01:57:56,072 --> 01:58:00,502
the guard Alps will be poisoned before the
attack and they won't be able to fight.

862
01:58:00,783 --> 01:58:03,473
What about the secret passage, Helen?

863
01:58:03,639 --> 01:58:06,449
You and your soldiers go into
the secret passage from here.

864
01:58:06,449 --> 01:58:08,189
And I'll open the door for you.

865
01:58:08,392 --> 01:58:11,052
They won't have time to use their swords.

866
01:58:11,509 --> 01:58:17,269
When Kayıs handle with Geyhatu, we'll
take our Kulucahisar back.

867
01:58:29,826 --> 01:58:33,826
Don't you have a place for
the Roman Emperor?

868
01:58:44,688 --> 01:58:48,178
Roma is little.

869
01:58:54,137 --> 01:58:57,277
Mongols are big.

870
01:59:06,937 --> 01:59:09,337
You'll wait standing.

871
01:59:15,412 --> 01:59:19,412
Roma is big, Geyhatu.
Big.

872
01:59:19,877 --> 01:59:21,657
You can't handle...

873
01:59:24,201 --> 01:59:25,641
lots of Turkmen.

874
01:59:28,450 --> 01:59:29,860
Wait standing.

875
01:59:33,949 --> 01:59:37,949
Do you know why I summon you?

876
01:59:42,694 --> 01:59:45,464
It must be something important, Geyhatu.

877
01:59:45,687 --> 01:59:48,697
Important or not.

878
01:59:50,771 --> 01:59:53,681
You'll come when I summon you.

879
02:00:03,105 --> 02:00:06,095
Important or not, Geyhatu.

880
02:00:07,412 --> 02:00:09,482
Why did you summon me?

881
02:00:11,266 --> 02:00:12,686
I'm going to...

882
02:00:13,764 --> 02:00:16,014
the Kayı tribe.

883
02:00:18,747 --> 02:00:21,697
I will kill...

884
02:00:23,257 --> 02:00:24,907
Ertuğrul and his daughters.

885
02:00:27,404 --> 02:00:29,974
And you will...

886
02:00:31,524 --> 02:00:35,764
get Kulucahisar back.

887
02:00:43,961 --> 02:00:46,361
That's an important thing.

888
02:00:47,541 --> 02:00:50,501
I like important news.

889
02:00:51,189 --> 02:00:52,899
You look for a place to sit.

890
02:00:54,159 --> 02:00:56,859
Go sit in Kulucahisar.

891
02:01:01,053 --> 02:01:03,023
I will.

892
02:01:04,428 --> 02:01:06,698
Come on.
Go.

893
02:01:22,761 --> 02:01:24,881
Victory will be ours.

894
02:01:26,370 --> 02:01:28,250
Victory is ours!

895
02:02:13,345 --> 02:02:14,935
Savcı said...

896
02:02:16,163 --> 02:02:18,773
he'd bring me my son.

897
02:02:19,955 --> 02:02:21,685
Where is Savcı?

898
02:02:23,438 --> 02:02:25,058
Where is my son?

899
02:02:28,008 --> 02:02:30,008
Where is Osman...

900
02:02:30,217 --> 02:02:32,887
the filthy Turk?

901
02:02:34,112 --> 02:02:35,362
Geyhatu.

902
02:02:35,930 --> 02:02:38,820
Let's talk in the tent.

903
02:02:39,509 --> 02:02:41,969
If you say one more word...

904
02:02:42,584 --> 02:02:46,754
I'll kill you first, Yavlak.

905
02:02:50,464 --> 02:02:54,464
We sent my nephew to you as an envoy.

906
02:02:54,888 --> 02:02:57,088
Don't you trust our words?

907
02:02:57,808 --> 02:03:00,978
Osman abducted my son.

908
02:03:01,573 --> 02:03:05,573
My nephew Osman doesn't
abduct his enemies.

909
02:03:05,870 --> 02:03:07,640
He kills them.

910
02:03:12,224 --> 02:03:15,404
If he's innocent, then where is he?

911
02:03:16,643 --> 02:03:18,423
He should come!

912
02:03:19,415 --> 02:03:20,845
He went after Savcı.

913
02:03:20,992 --> 02:03:23,632
Savcı said he'd bring...

914
02:03:23,632 --> 02:03:26,342
my son in three days!

915
02:03:26,693 --> 02:03:28,163
Three days...

916
02:03:28,409 --> 02:03:31,479
is when the sun goes down.

917
02:03:32,922 --> 02:03:37,342
I'll kill all of the Turks on these lands!

918
02:03:51,150 --> 02:03:52,430
Geyhatu...

919
02:03:53,599 --> 02:03:57,599
if you want war, let's fight.

920
02:04:00,708 --> 02:04:03,098
Maybe you wreck our tribe...

921
02:04:03,098 --> 02:04:06,288
you kill us or maybe...

922
02:04:06,298 --> 02:04:10,908
you take our heads off and go, but...

923
02:04:11,751 --> 02:04:14,811
it won't be easy.

924
02:04:16,716 --> 02:04:18,286
You'll be buried in a grave...

925
02:04:19,296 --> 02:04:22,346
with your dignity and with us.

926
02:04:40,223 --> 02:04:42,533
It's a good way...

927
02:04:42,693 --> 02:04:45,303
to die, Geyhatu.

928
02:04:45,860 --> 02:04:47,120
However...

929
02:04:47,276 --> 02:04:51,756
we don't know who the
death will take first.

930
02:04:51,970 --> 02:04:55,080
Don't, Geyhatu. Even if
Osman has done it...

931
02:04:55,080 --> 02:04:57,530
Kayıs don't know about it.

932
02:04:57,637 --> 02:05:00,177
They don't know what is Osman up to.

933
02:05:00,230 --> 02:05:04,720
Let me handle it.
I kept every word of mine.

934
02:05:05,032 --> 02:05:06,672
Enough!

935
02:05:07,577 --> 02:05:12,057
Osman Bey is coming!
Osman Bey is coming!

936
02:05:33,733 --> 02:05:35,043
My Osman.

937
02:05:41,784 --> 02:05:43,314
Osman!

938
02:05:49,215 --> 02:05:52,405
May Allah protect you, my Bey!

939
02:06:38,836 --> 02:06:40,466
Osman!

940
02:06:41,775 --> 02:06:43,125
Alps!

941
02:06:55,323 --> 02:06:57,923
Tell us what you saw.

942
02:06:58,086 --> 02:07:01,596
We saw some things.

943
02:07:01,914 --> 02:07:03,814
We have some bad news.

944
02:07:04,064 --> 02:07:06,894
Geyhatu has gathered his army and...

945
02:07:07,610 --> 02:07:09,320
is going to Kayı tribe.

946
02:07:11,336 --> 02:07:13,286
He won't wait.

947
02:07:34,316 --> 02:07:37,366
Geyhatu and his soldiers have
come a long way.

948
02:07:38,591 --> 02:07:41,941
They should drink our cold Ayran and rest.

949
02:07:54,584 --> 02:07:57,124
We offer you our cold Ayran while...

950
02:07:58,611 --> 02:08:02,111
you offer us blood, Geyhatu.

951
02:08:03,820 --> 02:08:05,650
Where is my son, Osman?

952
02:08:12,213 --> 02:08:14,293
The son who doesn't know the ancestors...

953
02:08:15,459 --> 02:08:18,099
don't deserve anything.

954
02:08:19,621 --> 02:08:21,951
When they are in the womb...

955
02:08:22,815 --> 02:08:24,885
they born.

956
02:08:30,088 --> 02:08:31,948
I think you shouldn't call the name...

957
02:08:32,922 --> 02:08:36,922
of your son who isn't appropriate
for your ancestor Genghis Khan.

958
02:08:38,638 --> 02:08:40,958
It's not a good manner, Geyhatu.

959
02:08:42,138 --> 02:08:44,078
Osman...

960
02:08:46,752 --> 02:08:49,852
I'll kill you, Turk!

961
02:08:49,880 --> 02:09:07,600
Please contact us for any inquiries
turkision@gmail.com